   {
    "id": "t38_n3",
    "type": "flograph.util.note",
    "pos": [
     0,
     2960
    ],
    "params": {
     "text": "## 3 · Regression — predict a number\n\n**Train Model** learns `price_k` from every other number column of the\n**train** rows (text like `band` is left out on its own). *Ridge* is a\nstraight-line model that resists over-fitting; swap the *Algorithm* to\n*random forest* and compare. **Feature importances** shows what it leans\non.\n\n**Predict** runs the trained model — the **model** wire is the whole fitted\nmodel as a value — over the **test** rows, adding a `prediction` column.\n\n**Model Evaluation** compares `price_k` with `prediction` on rows the model\nnever saw:\n\n* **MAE** — the typical miss, in the target's own units (£k here).\n* **RMSE** — the same, but big misses count extra. Much bigger than MAE =\n  a few bad misses.\n* **R²** — share of the variation explained: 1 is perfect, 0 is no better\n  than guessing the average for every house.\n\nOn the chart a perfect model sits on the dashed line. Hover a point to see\nthe house it missed.",
     "width": 620,
     "height": 640
    },
    "code": null,
    "label": null
   },
