    ],
    "params": {
     "text": "## 4 · Classification — predict a class\n\nSame rows, a different question: which **band** is the house in? The\ntarget is text, so the task is read as *classification*. `price_k` is\nnamed out of the features on purpose — it *is* the answer in disguise, and\na model that peeks at it scores 100% and is useless.\n\n*Random forest* needs no scaling and copes with mixed features; it is a\nstrong first choice for classification.\n\n**Predict** with *Add probabilities* gives one column per band: how sure\nthe model is. Sort by it to find the houses it nearly got wrong.\n\n**Model Evaluation** now shows a **confusion matrix**: actual bands down\nthe side, predictions across. The diagonal is right; everything else is a\nmix-up — and mix-ups between *neighbouring* bands are the forgivable kind.\n*Normalize* shows each row as shares, so a weak band stands out.\n\n* **accuracy** — share predicted right.\n* **precision** — when it says \"over 450k\", how often is it?\n* **recall** — of the real \"over 450k\" houses, how many did it find?\n* **F1** — one number balancing the two.",
     "width": 620,
     "height": 680
    },
    "code": null,
    "label": null
   },
   {
    "id": "t38_tr4",
    "type": "flograph.util.goto_from",
    "pos": [
     760,
     4060
    ],
    "params": {
     "source": "t38_pub_tr"
    },
    "code": null,
    "label": "train →"
   },
   {
    "id": "t38_te4",
    "type": "flograph.util.goto_from",
    "pos": [
     760,
     4340
    ],
    "params": {
     "source": "t38_pub_te"
    },
    "code": null,
    "label": "test →"
   },
   {
    "id": "t38_cls",
    "type": "flograph.ml.train_model",
    "pos": [
     1020,
     4040
    ],
    "params": {
     "target_column": "band",
     "algorithm": "random forest",
     "feature_columns": "size_m2, rooms, age_years, garden, city_Leeds, city_York",
     "trees": 200
    },
    "code": null,
    "label": "Train Model (band)"
   },
   {
    "id": "t38_cls_pred",
    "type": "flograph.ml.predict",
    "pos": [
     1280,
     4340
    ],
    "params": {
     "probability": true
    },
    "code": null,
    "label": "Predict (band)"
   },
   {
    "id": "t38_cls_eval",
    "type": "flograph.ml.model_evaluation",
    "pos": [
     1560,
     4000
    ],
    "params": {
     "actual_column": "band",
     "normalize": true,
     "width": 480,
     "height": 420
    },
    "code": null,
    "label": "Classification check"
   },
   {
    "id": "t38_cls_probs",
    "type": "flograph.viz.show_table",
    "pos": [
     2100,
     4000
    ],
    "params": {
     "width": 360,
     "height": 420
    },
    "code": null,
    "label": "How sure it was"
   },
   {
    "id": "t38_n5",
    "type": "flograph.util.note",
    "pos": [
     0,
     4960
    ],
    "params": {
     "text": "## 5 · Is it really that good? Cross-validation\n\nOne train/test split is one roll of the dice: a lucky split flatters a\nmodel. **Cross-Validation** cuts the rows into 5 *folds*, trains on four\nand scores the fifth, five times over, and reports the mean and the spread\n(**std**).\n\nTwo side by side — *ridge* and *random forest*, same features, same folds\n— is how to choose an algorithm **before** training the one you keep.\nPrefer the higher mean R²; a big std means the score depends on which rows\nit got, which usually means too little data.\n\nCross-validation fits its own models each time, so it takes the cleaned\ntable straight from **houses** and names its features — text columns have\nto be encoded first, as in chapter 2.",
     "width": 620,
     "height": 520
    },
    "code": null,
    "label": null
   },
   {
    "id": "t38_from5",
    "type": "flograph.util.goto_from",
    "pos": [
     760,
     5160
    ],
    "params": {
     "source": "t38_pub"
    },
    "code": null,
    "label": "houses →"
   },
   {
    "id": "t38_cv_lin",
    "type": "flograph.ml.cross_validation",
    "pos": [
     1020,
     5000
    ],
    "params": {
     "target_column": "price_k",
     "algorithm": "ridge",
     "feature_columns": "size_m2, rooms, age_years, garden"
    },
    "code": null,
    "label": "Cross-validate ridge"
   },
   {
    "id": "t38_cv_rf",
    "type": "flograph.ml.cross_validation",
    "pos": [
     1020,
     5300
    ],
    "params": {
     "target_column": "price_k",
     "algorithm": "random forest",
     "feature_columns": "size_m2, rooms, age_years, garden",
     "trees": 100
    },
    "code": null,
    "label": "Cross-validate forest"
   },
   {
    "id": "t38_cv_lin_tbl",
    "type": "flograph.viz.show_table",
    "pos": [
     1280,
     4960
    ],
    "params": {
     "width": 440,
     "height": 200
    },
    "code": null,
    "label": "Ridge, 5 folds"
   },
   {
    "id": "t38_cv_rf_tbl",
    "type": "flograph.viz.show_table",
    "pos": [
     1280,
     5260
    ],
    "params": {
     "width": 440,
     "height": 200
    },
    "code": null,
    "label": "Forest, 5 folds"
   },
   {
    "id": "t38_n6",
    "type": "flograph.util.note",
    "pos": [
     0,
     5760
    ],
    "params": {
     "text": "## 6 · No target? Find groups with K-Means\n\nClustering has no answer column. **K-Means** puts each house with the\nnearest of *k* centres, moving the centres until they settle — groups of\nlook-alikes, found rather than labelled.\n\n* **Standardize** is on: without it, a column in hundreds (price) would\n  out-vote one in tens (rooms).\n* **k** is yours to choose. Try 2, 3, 4: the right one gives groups you\n  can *name* from the **centres** table (\"big and dear\", \"small, cheap\n  and old\"…).\n* The chart squashes the chosen columns to two directions so you can see\n  the groups; click one in the legend to hide it.\n\nThe `cluster` column comes back on **table** — feed it into chapter 3 as a\nfeature, or use it to filter a dashboard.",
     "width": 620,
     "height": 560
    },
    "code": null,
    "label": null
   },
   {
    "id": "t38_from6",
    "type": "flograph.util.goto_from",
    "pos": [
     760,
     5960
    ],
    "params": {
     "source": "t38_pub"
    },
    "code": null,
    "label": "houses →"
   },
   {
    "id": "t38_km",
    "type": "flograph.ml.kmeans_clustering",
    "pos": [
     1020,
     5760
    ],
    "params": {
     "k": 3,
     "columns": "size_m2, age_years, price_k",
     "width": 480,
     "height": 420
    },
    "code": null,
    "label": "Clusters"
   },
