  "pages": [
   {
    "id": "t38_report",
    "title": "ML tutorial",
    "kind": "report",
    "body": "# Machine learning in flograph\n\nA short read through the flow on the canvas, with its live results. Every\nchart and table below is a node in that flow — change the data or a\nsetting there and this page follows.\n\n## The data\n\nOne row per house sale, one column per measurement: the tidy table every\nML node expects. Size is the strongest clue to price:\n\n![[Correlation|width=80%]]\n\nOne price had an extra zero. Outlier Detection flagged it and the rest of\nthe flow works on the table without it.\n\n## Predicting the price (regression)\n\nTrained on three quarters of the houses, scored on the quarter it never\nsaw. Points near the dashed line are good guesses:\n\n![[Regression check|width=80%]]\n\n![[Regression scores]]\n\n## Predicting the band (classification)\n\nThe diagonal is right; off it are mix-ups, mostly between neighbouring\nbands:\n\n![[Classification check|width=80%]]\n\n## How much to trust it\n\nFive folds, two algorithms — the mean is the score, the std is the luck:\n\n![[Ridge, 5 folds]]\n\n![[Forest, 5 folds]]\n\n## Groups nobody labelled\n\n![[Clusters|width=80%]]\n\n![[Cluster centres]]\n",
    "tiles": []
   }
  ]
 }
}